From 0349fd0d539a25683bf0fb4387d50216f99c9c69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:41:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/28] (b) v2, part b-3: no duplicate target for a caption
 that does not step

With \@captionstepfalse alone (the documented continued-float case) the
kernel plug of caption/step still used refstepcounter/target with the
unchanged counter. hyperref then made a second destination with the name
of the last stepped caption ("destination with the same identifier",
duplicate ignored), and \ref to the continued caption led to the first
one. caption-interface-001 recorded that as expected (review finding H3).

Now a caption that does not step its counter gets the float target
(\@floatHref@<type>, unchanged) or, if there is none, a target with a
unique name: \@caption@uniquetarget gives \theH<counter> the suffix
*<n> (n counts these targets) inside a group around the socket
refstepcounter/target, so hyperref names it <counter>.<theH>*<n>, e.g.
figure.1*1 (hyperref does not use * in \theH<counter>), and the kernel
plug sets that name. \label after a continued caption gives the number
of the counter and a link to the continued caption itself.
\@captiontargetfalse still makes no target.

The target is made by the same socket as for stepped captions, so
nothing changes in the typeset output: an anonymous \MakeLinkTarget
(tried first) adds a whatsit without hyperref, which moved a caption by
0.5pt in the caption suite (issues/gitlab/issue_38, picinpar).

Tests: caption-interface-001 test 8 now expects the unique name; new
tests for a continued caption with a float target, without target, and
two continued captions. float-023 (tagging + hyperref) gets continued
captions outside of floats and in a float. New float-024 uses the real
hyperref plugs without \DocumentMetadata (hyperref told not to patch
\caption): the base suite cannot load hyperref.
